  "notes": "The kanji {贔屓|ひいき} are rarely written; hiragana is very common.\n\nCOMMON PATTERNS:\n- {贔屓|ひいき}にする: to patronize, to favor\n- {贔屓|ひいき}のお{店|みせ}: one's favorite shop\n- {贔屓|ひいき}のチーム: one's favorite team\n- ご{贔屓|ひいき}に: please continue to patronize us (business)\n\nCOMMON EXPRESSIONS:\n- {贔屓|ひいき}の{引|ひ}き{倒|たお}し: doing more harm than good by being overly supportive\n\nUSAGE:\nWhen used about one's own favorites, it's positive (patronage, support). When used about others showing favoritism, it can be negative (unfair bias).",
